1
00:03:41,250 --> 00:03:47,250
Man has made his match... now it's his problem.

2
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:28,500
Blade Runner is a science fiction, drama,
thriller film directed by Ridley Scott.

3
00:11:03,750 --> 00:11:09,750
In the smog-choked dystopian Los Angeles of 2019, blade runner Rick Deckard is called out of retirement to terminate a
quartet of replicants who have escaped to Earth seeking their creator for a way to extend their short life spans.

4
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:51,000
Deckard, played by Harrison Ford.

5
00:18:26,250 --> 00:18:32,250
Batty, played by Rutger Hauer.

6
00:22:07,500 --> 00:22:13,500
Rachael, played by Sean Young.

7
00:25:48,750 --> 00:25:54,750
Gaff, played by Edward James Olmos.

8
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:36,000
Bryant, played by M. Emmet Walsh.

9
00:33:11,250 --> 00:33:17,250
Pris, played by Daryl Hannah.

10
00:36:52,500 --> 00:36:58,500
Blade Runner is a 1982 science fiction film directed by Ridley Scott
from a screenplay by Hampton Fancher and David Peoples.

11
00:40:33,750 --> 00:40:39,750
Starring Harrison Ford, Rutger Hauer, Sean Young, and Edward
James Olmos, it is an adaptation of Philip K.

12
00:44:15,000 --> 00:44:21,000
Dick's 1968 novel Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep?

13
00:47:56,250 --> 00:48:02,250
The film is set in a dystopian future Los Angeles of 2019, in which synthetic humans known as
replicants are bio-engineered by the powerful Tyrell Corporation to work on space colonies.

14
00:51:37,500 --> 00:51:43,500
When a fugitive group of advanced replicants led by Roy Batty (Hauer) escapes back to
Earth, former cop Rick Deckard (Ford) reluctantly agrees to hunt them down.

15
00:55:18,750 --> 00:55:24,750
Blade Runner initially underperformed in North American theaters and polarized critics; some praised its
thematic complexity and visuals, while others critiqued its slow pacing and lack of action.

16
00:59:00,000 --> 00:59:06,000
The film's soundtrack, composed by Vangelis, was nominated in 1982
for a BAFTA and a Golden Globe as best original score.

17
01:02:41,250 --> 01:02:47,250
Blade Runner later became a cult film, and has since come to be
regarded as one of the greatest science fiction films.

18
01:06:22,500 --> 01:06:28,500
Hailed for its production design depicting a high-tech but decaying future, the film is often regarded as
both a leading example of neo-noir cinema and a foundational work of the cyberpunk genre.

19
01:10:03,750 --> 01:10:09,750
It has influenced many science fiction films, video
games, anime, and television series.

20
01:13:45,000 --> 01:13:51,000
It also brought the work of Dick to Hollywood's attention and
led to several film adaptations of his works.

21
01:17:26,250 --> 01:17:32,250
In 1993, it was selected for preservation in the National
Film Registry by the Library of Congress.

22
01:21:07,500 --> 01:21:13,500
Seven different versions of Blade Runner exist as a result of
controversial changes requested by studio executives.

23
01:24:48,750 --> 01:24:54,750
A director's cut was released in 1992 after a strong
response to test screenings of a workprint.

24
01:28:30,000 --> 01:28:36,000
This, in conjunction with the film's popularity as a video rental,
made it one of the earliest films to be released on DVD.

25
01:32:11,250 --> 01:32:17,250
In 2007, Warner Bros.

26
01:35:52,500 --> 01:35:58,500
released The Final Cut, a 25th-anniversary digitally remastered version; this
is the only version over which Scott retained artistic control.

27
01:39:33,750 --> 01:39:39,750
The film is the first of the franchise of the same name.

28
01:43:15,000 --> 01:43:21,000
A sequel, titled Blade Runner 2049, was released in 2017 alongside a trilogy of short
films covering the thirty-year span between the two films' settings.

29
01:46:56,250 --> 01:47:02,250
The anime series Blade Runner: Black Lotus was released in 2021.

30
01:50:37,500 --> 01:50:43,500
The film explores themes of android, flying car, bounty
hunter, artificial intelligence (a.i.), genetics.

31
01:54:18,750 --> 01:54:24,750
The tone is intense and dark and thought_provoking.
